Z||000048||tgowens||07-16-2000||06:23 PM||||hey Spyder, it looked fine the <I>first</I> time!!!<P>Al, if you just want to show everyone the photo, like Stimpy said, use url inside the [] and [/] instead of (img) you are trying to put in a page rather than an image by using the http:// thing.........-- it makes all the difference in the world.......if you are trying use it as a signature, you will have to do much more....let me know which you want to do and i'll try to help you with it......<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">             <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000049||AL||07-18-2000||01:13 AM||||twogen i already have my signature in,but if i want to post the pic like you all what do i have to do?if ichange my signature then i lose my pic on my email so what do i do?||||reg||5
Z||000050||tgowens||07-18-2000||03:10 AM||||Al, upload the image to your server, then in the signature box of your profile put in IMG enclosed by [ and ] and then put the <A HREF="http://www.xxxxx.com/xxx/image.gif" TARGET=_blank>http://www.xxxxx.com/xxx/image.gif</A>  and end it with /IMG enclosed by [ and ] -- you don't have to replace your signature - just add the image to it........on mine, the image is one part and the link to my web site is the other part........<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">               <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
